.SS procs
.TP
.B R
Number of runnable processes (running or queued for CPU).
.TP
.B B
Number of processes in uninterruptible sleep (typically blocked on
disk I/O).
.SS memory
.TP
.B SWPD
Amount of virtual memory currently swapped out, in the chosen unit.
.TP
.B FREE
Amount of idle memory (kernel \fBMemFree\fR).
.TP
.B BUFF
Memory used as kernel buffers. Replaced by \fBINACT\fR under \fB\-a\fR.
.TP
.B CACHE
Page cache plus reclaimable slab memory (\fBCached\fR +
\fBSReclaimable\fR). Replaced by \fBACTIVE\fR under \fB\-a\fR.
.TP
.B INACT
(\fB\-a\fR only) Inactive memory — pages not recently referenced.
.TP
.B ACTIVE
(\fB\-a\fR only) Active memory — recently-used pages.
.SS swap
.TP
.B SI
Memory swapped in from disk per second, in the unit selected by \fB\-S\fR.
.TP
.B SO
Memory swapped out to disk per second, in the unit selected by \fB\-S\fR.
.SS io
.TP
.B BI
Blocks read from block devices per second.
.TP
.B BO
Blocks written to block devices per second.
.SS system
.TP
.B IN
Interrupts per second, including the timer interrupt.
.TP
.B CS
Context switches per second.
.SS cpu
.PP
The CPU columns are percentages of total CPU time:
.TP
.B US
User-space (non-nice) time.
.TP
.B SY
Kernel-space (system) time.
.TP
.B ID
Idle time, excluding I/O wait.
.TP
.B WA
Time waiting for I/O completion.
.TP
.B ST
Time stolen from this VM by the hypervisor.
.TP
.B GU
Time spent running a guest VM (when this host is the hypervisor).
